<title>FRANCE: MATIF group rejects more Ecu products pre-1999.</title>
<headline>MATIF group rejects more Ecu products pre-1999.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A working group set up to look at how the MATIF futures and options exchange should position itself for the planned introduction of the euro in 1999 rejected a strategy of developing products denominated in Ecus.</p>
<p>In a report published on Wednesday, the group said, &quot;The members of the working committee have reservations about the future of the Ecu between now and 1999 and reject a...strategy based on developing a range of Ecu products on MATIF ahead of the transition to the euro.</p>
<p>&quot;Publication during 1998 of the list of states joining EMU (European Monetary Union) in the first wave could perhaps revive interest in the Ecu,&quot; the report said.</p>
<p>&quot;However, to launch new Ecu products immediately would certainly expose MATIF to the risk of a setback which could prove costly for the market's credibility,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
